  "id": "implicit-process",
  "term": "implicit process",
  "definition": "An implicit process is an underlying psychological pathway that shapes behavior without being directly visible in the interaction itself. In this source, it refers to internal processes such as a parent’s interpretation of a child’s signals or the influence of the parent’s beliefs on how the parent responds.",
